# Tenant Isolation

Every tenant-owned row and query must be scoped by server-derived `tenant_id`.

## Required

- Resolve tenant from auth session, call-scope, or worker job row — never from free-form body/query alone
- All repos filter `WHERE tenant_id = :tenant_id` (or equivalent join)
- Uniqueness and indexes that are business-local include `tenant_id`
- Workers set `TenantContext` from the claimed row before touching tenant data
- Object keys are tenant-prefixed: `tenants/{tenant_id}/...`

## Forbidden

```text
# ❌ Client supplies tenant and server trusts it
GET /resources?tenant_id=<attacker>

# ❌ Cross-tenant fetch by bare id
session.get(Model, id)  # without tenant check
```

```text
# ✅ Server scope + id
repo.get(tenant_id=scope.tenant_id, id=resource_id)
```

Cross-tenant access must fail closed (403/404). Add or extend isolation tests when touching tenant data paths.

See: `docs/TENANCY_ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/DATA_OWNERSHIP.md`
